▶ one mutant per state, each proven non-vacuous
  ✔ holds no-record: a mutant that joins a string as a record reddens (1.6962ms)
  ℹ the no-record guard skips parsing and joins the string -> NO-RECORD PARSE: a record that does not parse must state no-record, never a state read off a string
  ✔ holds declared: a mutant that never declares reddens (1.0983ms)
  ℹ the declared state is removed and a declaration answers no-node -> DECLARED: a record carrying the node and the input it read must state declared, never no-node
  ✔ holds no-node: a mutant that cannot tell an absent schema from a gap reddens (0.88ms)
  ℹ the no-node branch is removed and an absent schema answers cannot-tell -> NO-NODE: the committed record states the schema is absent, so a field it carries no node for must state no-node, never cannot-tell — an absent schema is a measurement, not a failure of the field
  ✔ holds cannot-tell: a mutant that upgrades a node without its input reddens (0.8896ms)
  ℹ the input that node read is no longer required to declare -> CANNOT-TELL: a record that names a node and records no input for it must state cannot-tell, never declared
  ✔ holds the single list: a mutant that reads a fifth field reddens (0.5834ms)
  ℹ the no-node branch stops asking the one list whether it reads the field -> SINGLE LIST: a field outside the declared list must state cannot-tell, never no-node — the join reads four field names and no fifth
  ✔ holds the row: a mutant that copies the facts into observed reddens (1.5353ms)
  ℹ observed is taken from the facts instead of the record row -> INVENTED STATE: observed must be the record row copied unchanged, never what the facts carry
  ✔ holds the input: a mutant that reads presence as truth reddens (0.8499ms)
  ℹ a recorded input of false is treated as no input -> INPUT PRESENCE: a node whose input was recorded as false read something, so it must state declared, never cannot-tell
✔ one mutant per state, each proven non-vacuous (7.7881ms)
